# Support

Thank you for your interest in the **Diabetes Metabolic Model**.

This project is developed as an open educational resource to help improve the understanding of diabetes physiology.

## How You Can Support the Project

You can contribute by:

* Reporting errors or inaccuracies.
* Suggesting improvements.
* Improving diagrams and visualizations.
* Reviewing the educational content.
* Translating the documentation into other languages.
* Sharing the project with healthcare professionals, educators, and people living with diabetes.
* Contributing scientific references and educational resources.

## Feedback

Constructive feedback is always welcome.

If you identify unclear explanations or believe a concept can be presented more accurately, please open a GitHub Issue or submit a Pull Request.

## Medical Community

Healthcare professionals, researchers, educators, and students are encouraged to participate in improving the educational quality of this repository.

## Open Knowledge

The goal of this project is to promote open access to educational knowledge while encouraging respectful collaboration and evidence-based discussion.

Thank you for supporting this project.

